## Archive the run

Any run that justifies a promotion is archived next to its evidence. **File it under the
dated build tag** (e.g. `server-dev-b11158-1-20260924-2006`) in `benchmark/` of the image's
repo — never under a pointer like `stable` or `server-dev`, which move and would leave the
directory describing something else. If the run was performed through a pointer, say which
dated tag it resolved to at the time.

Record the digest of **every moving part**: the backend image, the harness image, and any
model or drafter pulled by tag rather than by digest. The digest in the report and the tag in
the directory must agree.

Contents: `REPORT.md`, the T1/T2 outputs with the code fence stripped (so they open as
documents), and the A1-A3 sessions in **both** forms — `.jsonl.zstd` byte-exact as dsh wrote
it, and decompressed `.jsonl` so it can be read without tooling. A `.lock` sibling is not
part of the log. New builds **add** a directory; never overwrite one.

Sessions contain whatever the agent read, and they go into a repository. Scan before
committing:

```bash
grep -rlE 'ghp_[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}|github_pat_|sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|Bearer [A-Za-z0-9._-]{20,}|hf_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}' .
```

Expect hits when a task reviews source code (`Authorization`, `password`, `passwd` in
excerpts and in path-traversal analysis) — read each one, and do not skip the scan.
